{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F4iS9swg5Rx3RJG5qNocwa","type":"tool_result","content":"```\n\n`ard init` opens a pull request with the starter `.ard/` tree: `config.yaml` and the starter role directories. Review and merge it. Then:\n\n```sh\n| `merge.protected_paths` | none | A pull request touching any entry waits for human approval. There is no built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in `/` is a directory prefix, anything else is a glob |\n\n`ard init` writes a recommended list that includes `.github/`, `.ard/config.yaml`, the role directories, `CODEOWNERS`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/`, `.mcp.json` and build and deploy files.\n\n\n## Upgrades\n\nBuild the new `ard`, stop `ard serve` and start the new binary. Run `ard config check` first, because a new release may reject a key the old one accepted. Review the release for changes to the starter roles; `ard init` proposes updates as a pull request and never deletes.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9fc659e-2b79-4850-b189-0bda8f59ffda","uuid":"b20570b6-c993-43eb-b979-49ae9db5bd06","timestamp":"2026-11-25T08:11:49.402Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"```\n\n`ard init` opens a pull request with the starter `.ard/` tree: `config.yaml` and the starter role directories. Review and merge it. Then:\n\n```sh\n| `merge.protected_paths` | none | A pull request touching any entry waits for human approval. There is no built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in `/` is a directory prefix, anything else is a glob |\n\n`ard init` writes a recommended list that includes `.github/`, `.ard/config.yaml`, the role directories, `CODEOWNERS`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/`, `.mcp.json` and build and deploy files.\n\n\n## Upgrades\n\nBuild the new `ard`, stop `ard serve` and start the new binary. Run `ard config check` first, because a new release may reject a key the old one accepted. Review the release for changes to the starter roles; `ard init` proposes updates as a pull request and never deletes.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F4iS9swg5Rx3RJG5qNocwa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
